Z||000000||Formula88||03-26-2001||01:01 AM||||I've read a lot of posts about people using the 4 speed Muncie witht the 4.10 gears for better performance.  That's well and good, but I wouldn't want to sacrifice my 5th gear.  Is there any way to put a 4.10 gear in the 5-speed Getrag?  Are different gear ratios even available?  A 4.10 gear with a 5 speed would rock!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||03-26-2001||01:25 AM||||I talked to a tranny rebuilder about doing this sort of thing(he's got a turbo dieself VW engine in his '86 coupe!"  He told me that it would NOT work using Isuzu to Getrag.  4.10 gear are FUN for around town.  You just can't beat the off-the-line punch.  Highway is so-so....<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||03-26-2001||10:04 AM||||I'm not trying to hybrid Muncie 4speed or Isuzu 5-speed parts into the Getrag.  My question is if there are any 4.10 or so gearsets available for the Getrag.  I've heard that Mantapart has replacement gear sets, but I don't know what ratio.  I'll check them out later.||||reg||1
Z||000003||owenslee||03-26-2001||01:08 PM||||Formula 88,<P>The Manta gearsets for the Getrag are 3.94<P>Those are the lowest final ratio I am aware of for the Getrag.<P>They came originally in the Getrag "New Venture" 5 spd used in A body FWD cars (Beretta, Achieva, Grand Am ) using the Quad 4 engine. The RPO code was ( XTX) . <P>I believe that they were used  primarily in 93-94 cars but not certain.<P>Be aware that the 4th and 5th ratios in these transmissions were also different. (4th= 1.03  5th=.81 )<P>Hope that helps...<P>Kerry||||reg||7
Z||000004||Formula88||03-26-2001||01:13 PM||||Thanks!  That does help.  If/when I rebuild my Getrag, I may opt for the lower gearset.  Just the thing for those quick getaways from the Gas-N-Sip.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||03-26-2001||01:20 PM||||I was looking for a 3.94 from a Beretta GTZ but couldnt find one, so when I rebuild my tranny I am definitely getting the MantaPart gearing.  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||03-26-2001||01:22 PM||||Hey, man, no way! You can't do that!<BR>You'll get a quicker launch than me!<P>(Hell, at least if it works on yours, I'll know what to do to mine...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||03-28-2001||10:32 AM||||Yea, well, after checking out the Mantapart site, they want $800 for for 3.94 ring gear and pinion output shaft!!  Hell, they've got a complete Auburn style limited slip differential unit for the Getrag 282 for $750!  Doubt I'll be swapping in THOSE gears.  That's too much for just a gear change.  Besides, from what everyone's been telling me, once you up the power a bit, 1st gear becomes too short with the stock gearing.  This would only be a benefit on a stock 2.8 or 3.1 is my guess.  I'll save the money for my 3.4 buildup...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||11
